        "id": 1644679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-31T00:17:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How big are the batches? Should it be configurable with a parameter? Maybe the client only wants one at a time?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "80a3d63a08f3046c5238fc5c85dd452b60660a96",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da2b0f30_bf5e18de",
        "filename": "staging/security/see/storage/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/storage/IDir.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-01T21:34:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The existing interface, added in aosp/400306, has a limit, but it was only used during development and does not work anymore.",
      "parentUuid": "cc318b8c_42c0e3e0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "80a3d63a08f3046c5238fc5c85dd452b60660a96",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6eb5b4cd_e9cd190b",
        "filename": "staging/security/see/storage/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/storage/IDir.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962190
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-01T22:45:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current implementation uses a max batch size of 5. Added an arg so that clients can specify a smaller batch size.",
      "parentUuid": "cc318b8c_42c0e3e0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "80a3d63a08f3046c5238fc5c85dd452b60660a96",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8374f8ba_4a430514",
        "filename": "staging/security/see/storage/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/storage/IDir.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-09T02:13:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why? The C version returns as many entries as it can fit in a single message. I would think we want to preserve that default behavior for efficiency.",
      "parentUuid": "6eb5b4cd_e9cd190b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "80a3d63a08f3046c5238fc5c85dd452b60660a96",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f006336a_d5c5080f",
        "filename": "staging/security/see/storage/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/storage/IDir.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962190
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-13T00:09:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The C version is manually packing the message struct so it knows exactly how many bytes are left; I don\u0027t think there\u0027s a way for binder clients to have that fine-grained control. I picked 5 because that ensures that the AIDL handler doesn\u0027t allocate more bytes than the C version.",
      "parentUuid": "8374f8ba_4a430514",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 58
      },
